{
  "id": "C-GOLD-007",
  "title": "a response sequence is consumed in order and then fails closed",
  "kind": "data-plane",
  "traces": [
    "§44.7",
    "§40.7",
    "§43.3",
    "§12.7"
  ],
  "note": "Element 0 is consumed by the first selected invocation, element 1 by the second. There is no implicit repeat-last behavior: the third invocation fails with 409. The invocation counter is 3, not 2, because the counter increments on selection and a selection whose response then fails stays counted (§12.7, §40.6). That is what makes an extra call observable.",
